#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:3
msgid "`nix --repair-path` - re-download path from substituter"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--repair-path` _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:9
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--repair-path` attempts to “repair” the specified paths by "
"redownloading them using the available substituters. If no substitutes are "
"available, then repair is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:15
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:17
msgid ""
"During repair, there is a very small time window during which the old path "
"(if it exists) is moved out of the way and replaced with the new path. If "
"repair is interrupted in between, then the system may be left in a broken "
"state (e.g., if the path contains a critical system component like the GNU C "
"Library)."
msgstr ""

